<p>A technical SEO audit covers everything that happens before Google even reads your content: whether your pages can be crawled, indexed and loaded quickly enough to rank at all. For a small-business site, this is almost always where the real, fixable problems are hiding.</p>

<h2>What is included</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Crawl errors and broken internal links</li>
  <li>Indexing and sitemap issues: pages Google cannot find, or should not be finding</li>
  <li>Page speed and Core Web Vitals on mobile and desktop</li>
  <li>Mobile usability</li>
  <li>Structured data and schema markup</li>
  <li>Duplicate content, canonical tags and, for multi-country sites, hreflang</li>
  <li>GA4 and Search Console setup with consent requirements in mind for GDPR markets</li>
</ul>

<p>Every audit ends with the fixes already made where possible, and a clear list of anything that needs a decision from you, not just a list of problems handed back.</p>
